# Citation File Format 1.2.0. GitHub reads this file and offers a "Cite this
# repository" button from it; `cffconvert` turns it into BibTeX or APA.
# Reference: https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# `doi` is the concept DOI, which Zenodo mints once per deposition and resolves
# to whichever version is newest. The per-version DOI of 0.8.0 is
# 10.5281/zenodo.21997390, and a citation carrying that sends a reader to 0.8.0
# no matter what they ran. Neither is derivable from the version, so the
# per-version one cannot be a bump site the way `version` below is: Zenodo mints
# a fresh number on each deposit. The concept DOI needs no maintenance, which is
# the whole reason to prefer it here.
#
# `date-released` is deliberately absent. It would be a second thing the release
# bump has to rewrite, and it is the kind of field that goes stale silently.
# `version` below is a version site listed in `[tool.bumpversion.files]`, so it
# moves with every bump and
# `test_each_configured_pattern_is_in_the_file_it_points_at` fails if this file
# ever stops carrying it in the shape the bump expects. The release date a
# citation needs is on the tag and in CHANGELOG.md, both of which are gated; a
# copy here would be a third claim with nothing checking it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use figure-gate in published work, please cite it as below."
title: figure-gate
abstract: >-
  Mechanical gates for publication figures: colorblind-safe color, composition,
  and type legibility at print size. Every check reads the rendered figure's own
  artists, so a verdict is a measurement rather than a design opinion.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Prakash
    given-names: Naren
    email: 146764727+narenp12@users.noreply.github.com
version: 0.10.0.dev0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21784217
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/narenp12/figure-gate"
url: "https://narenp12.github.io/figure-gate/"
keywords:
  - matplotlib
  - figures
  - accessibility
  - colorblind
  - okabe-ito
  - viridis
  - data-visualization
  - publishing
